Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• HISTORY_NODES."id": primary key of each historical node; join key.  
• HISTORY_NODES."username": name of the mapper who created / last edited the node; grouping key.  
• HISTORY_NODES."latitude", HISTORY_NODES."longitude": numeric coordinates used to restrict the search to the requested rectangle.  
• HISTORY_NODES."all_tags": VARIANT array that can contain the object {"key":"amenity","value":"hospital | clinic | doctors"} – used to recognise the required amenities.  

• PLANET_NODES."id": list of the currently‑existing node ids; used to exclude nodes that “do not appear anymore”.  


Example exploration queries  
(Each query is wrapped in a code block, preceded by a short comment. Every column name is enclosed in double quotes, the database/schema/table names are adapted exactly to what is supplied, and every query returns at most 20 rows.)

```sql
--Description: 1) Quick peek at a few historical nodes and their tags
SELECT 
  t."id",
  t."username",
  t."latitude",
  t."longitude",
  t."all_tags"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Flatten the VARIANT column to view key / value pairs that live in "all_tags"
SELECT 
  t."id",
  f.value:"key"::STRING  AS "tag_key",
  f.value:"value"::STRING AS "tag_value"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show only those historical tags whose key equals 'amenity'
SELECT
  t."id",
  t."username",
  f.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity_value"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING ILIKE '%amenity%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Restrict historical nodes to the requested rectangular extent
SELECT
  t."id",
  t."username",
  t."latitude",
  t."longitude"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t
WHERE TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."longitude") BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."latitude")  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Nodes inside the rectangle AND tagged with amenity = hospital / clinic / doctors
SELECT
  t."id",
  t."username",
  f.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity_value",
  t."latitude",
  t."longitude"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING  = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%hospital%','%clinic%','%doctors%')
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."longitude") BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."latitude")  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Distinct ids of those amenity nodes in the rectangle
SELECT DISTINCT
  t."id"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t,
     LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING  = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%hospital%','%clinic%','%doctors%')
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."longitude") BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."latitude")  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Confirm whether a sample of those historical ids still exist in current PLANET_NODES
SELECT
  h."id"                        AS "hist_id",
  CASE WHEN p."id" IS NULL THEN 'NOT_IN_PLANET' ELSE 'STILL_EXISTS' END AS "current_status"
FROM (
    SELECT DISTINCT t."id"
    FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t,
         LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
    WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING  = 'amenity'
      AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%hospital%','%clinic%','%doctors%')
      AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."longitude") BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
      AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."latitude")  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
) h
LEFT JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_NODES" p
       ON h."id" = p."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Historical nodes of interest that are NOT in PLANET_NODES any longer
SELECT
  t."id",
  t."username",
  f.value:"value"::STRING AS "amenity_value"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t
JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
  ON TRUE
LEFT JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_NODES" p
  ON t."id" = p."id"
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING  = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%hospital%','%clinic%','%doctors%')
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."longitude") BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."latitude")  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND p."id" IS NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Count those “vanished” amenity nodes by username (top 20)
SELECT
  t."username",
  COUNT(*) AS "vanished_nodes"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t
JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
  ON TRUE
LEFT JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_NODES" p
  ON t."id" = p."id"
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING  = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%hospital%','%clinic%','%doctors%')
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."longitude") BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."latitude")  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND p."id" IS NULL
GROUP BY t."username"
ORDER BY "vanished_nodes" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final query – fetch the top three usernames with most vanished amenity nodes
SELECT
  t."username",
  COUNT(*) AS "vanished_nodes"
FROM "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."HISTORY_NODES" t
JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => t."all_tags") f
  ON TRUE
LEFT JOIN "GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."GEO_OPENSTREETMAP"."PLANET_NODES" p
  ON t."id" = p."id"
WHERE f.value:"key"::STRING  = 'amenity'
  AND f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%hospital%','%clinic%','%doctors%')
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."longitude") BETWEEN 31.1798246 AND 54.3798246
  AND TRY_TO_DOUBLE(t."latitude")  BETWEEN 18.4519921 AND 33.6519921
  AND p."id" IS NULL
GROUP BY t."username"
ORDER BY "vanished_nodes" DESC
LIMIT 3;
```
